      "content": "Medical experts universally agree that there is no safe margin for error with MAOIs and tyramine-rich foods; that is why the warnings are so extreme. There are no confirmed cases of partial consumption causing safe outcomes because the body lacks the enzyme needed to break down tyramine even at small doses. Even a tiny bite can trigger a panic attack, stroke, or death in individuals taking MAOIs, so portion control does not exist as a strategy. It is better to avoid confusion today than to risk a severe medical emergency tomorrow, so strict avoidance remains the only safe standard. You should stick to fresh, unaged, and unfermented proteins to stay safe.",
      "source": "target",
